Emerging Healthcare and Nutrition Trends
Maternal and infant healthcare is evolving toward preventive, nutrition-led interventions that support long-term cognitive and developmental outcomes. One of the most notable trends shaping the Algal DHA for maternal and infant market in 2025 is the rising shift toward sustainable, vegetarian, and pollutant-free omega-3 sources, positioning algal DHA as a preferred alternative to fish oil. Increasing integration of nutrition counseling into prenatal and postnatal care, combined with digital health education platforms, is further strengthening consumer understanding of DHA’s role in fetal brain, eye, and nervous system development.

